.TH FMD 1 "August 2026" "fmd" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fmd \- Fast, clean-room, dependency-lean Markdown to HTML & PDF renderer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fmd
[\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B fmd
[\fIINPUT\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIOUT\fR] [\fB\-\-to\fR \fIhtml|pdf|both|epub|svg\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B fmd
\fB\-\-text\fR \fI'# Hello'\fR [\fB\-o\fR \fIOUT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fmd
(franken_markdown) is a standalone CLI and pure-Rust library for rendering Markdown
into beautiful, self-contained HTML, compact deterministic PDF with embedded font subsets,
EPUB 3 e-books, and vector SVG posters.
.PP
It requires zero native system browser engines (no Headless Chrome, Chromium, or WebKit),
zero fontconfig or C library dependencies, and strictly forbids unsafe code.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
\fBrender\fR [\fIINPUT\fR]
Render a Markdown file (or stdin via \fB\-\fR) to HTML, PDF, EPUB, or SVG.
If the subcommand is omitted, \fBrender\fR is executed by default.
.TP
\fBcapabilities\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Print the machine-readable command, output format, exit code, and feature contract.
.TP
\fBrobot\-docs\fR [\fBguide\fR]
Print in-tool reference documentation formatted for coding agents and automated tools.
.TP
\fBverify\fR \fIINPUT\fR [\fB\-\-a11y\fR] [\fB\-\-links\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Audit a document's rendered text layer, internal headings and anchor integrity,
accessibility warnings, and horizontal margin overflow.
.TP
\fBwatch\fR \fIINPUT\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIOUT\fR [\fB\-\-serve\fR] [\fB\-\-interval\fR \fIMS\fR]
Watch a Markdown file and its referenced assets for changes, automatically re-rendering
and optionally serving an auto-reloading loopback preview.
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR [\fBfonts\fR \fB\-\-corpus\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Check local runtime capabilities, health status, and corpus glyph coverage against bundled fonts.
.TP
\fBconfig\fR [\fBshow\fR|\fBget\fR \fIKEY\fR|\fBset\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIVALUE\fR|\fBpath\fR]
Inspect or modify native configuration options (stored at \fI~/.config/fmd/config\fR).
.TP
\fBstats\fR [\fIINPUT\fR|\fB\-\-text\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Analyze document intelligence: word and character counts, reading/speaking time,
Flesch readability score, and heading outline hierarchy.
.TP
\fBdiff\fR \fIOLD_FILE\fR \fINEW_FILE\fR [\fB\-o\fR \fIOUT\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Perform structural semantic AST diffing between two documents and render a visual change report.
.TP
\fBbook\fR \fIDIR\fR [\fB\-o\fR \fIOUT_DIR\fR] [\fB\-\-to\fR \fIhtml|pdf|both\fR]
Assemble a multi-file directory into a unified multi-page HTML documentation site or single PDF book.
.TP
\fBbatch\fR \fIINPUTS...\fR [\fB\-\-out\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-to\fR \fITARGET\fR] [\fB\-\-workers\fR \fIN\fR]
Render many Markdown documents concurrently under a bounded worker pool and memory budget.
.TP
\fBmcp\fR [\fB\-\-max\-input\-bytes\fR \fIBYTES\fR]
Run Model Context Protocol (MCP) stdio server over JSON-RPC 2.0 exposing render, verify, and capabilities tools for AI coding agents.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit structured JSON on stdout (or status receipts on stderr during renders).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable decorative terminal styling and color output.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-config\fR
Bypass persistent configuration files for reproducible, config-free execution.
.TP
\fB\-\-robot\-triage\fR
Print a single-shot JSON envelope containing health status, quick commands, and next actions.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help information.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information.
.SH RENDER OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fIhtml|pdf|both|epub|svg\fR
Select output format (default: \fBhtml\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-out\fR \fIPATH\fR
Specify destination file path. \fB\-\fR writes HTML or SVG directly to stdout.
.TP
\fB\-\-font\fR \fIsans|serif\fR
Set default body typography family (default: \fBsans\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-font\-scale\fR, \fB\-\-type\-size\fR \fISCALE\fR
Uniform typographic scaling preset (\fBxs\fR, \fBsm\fR, \fBmd\fR, \fBlg\fR, \fBxl\fR, \fB2xl\fR),
percentage (\fB125%\fR), multiplier (\fB1.125\fR), or size (\fB18px\fR, \fB12pt\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-fit\-to\-pages\fR, \fB\-\-target\-pages\fR \fIPAGES\fR
Adaptive binary-search solver to fit PDF content strictly within \fIPAGES\fR page budget.
.TP
\fB\-\-microtype\fR \fIoff|protrusion|expansion|all\fR
Opt-in microtypography for justified PDF paragraphs: optical-margin hanging punctuation and font expansion.
.TP
\fB\-\-typography\-homogeneous\fR
Enable gradual adjacent demerits in Knuth-Plass optimal paragraph breaking.
.TP
\fB\-\-interactive\-html\fR, \fB\-\-self\-hosting\fR
Generate a self-hosting single-file HTML workspace with live editor, preview, and client-side PDF export.
.TP
\fB\-\-toc\fR
Generate a table of contents.
.TP
\fB\-\-toc\-depth\fR \fIN\fR
Maximum heading level depth included in table of contents (default: 3).
.TP
\fB\-\-pdf\-line\-numbers\fR
Display line numbers in PDF fenced code blocks.
.TP
\fB\-\-pdf\-page\-numbers\fR
Render running page numbers centered in the PDF bottom margin.
.TP
\fB\-\-pdf\-a\fR \fI2b\fR
Produce PDF/A-2b compliant archive with embedded sRGB ICC profile and XMP metadata packet.
.TP
\fB\-\-pdf\-a\-strict\fR
Fail closed on non-conformable PDF/A constructs (e.g. javascript/file URI schemes).
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-html\fR
Pass raw HTML markup through without escaping.
.TP
\fB\-\-css\fR \fIFILE\fR
Replace the default stylesheet with custom CSS.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success.
.TP
\fB64\fR
Command-line usage error or invalid flag arguments.
.TP
\fB66\fR
Input error (e.g. missing file, unreadable asset, or oversized input bytes).
.TP
\fB70\fR
Rendering error (e.g. font loading failure).
.TP
\fB73\fR
Output file error (e.g. cannot create directory or write target file).
.TP
\fB74\fR
Stdout write error (e.g. broken pipe).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Render a document to self-contained HTML:
.B fmd README.md \-o README.html
.TP
Render a document to high-quality PDF with page numbers:
.B fmd README.md \-\-to pdf \-\-pdf\-page\-numbers \-o README.pdf
.TP
Render raw Markdown text from stdin to stdout:
.B echo '# Hello World' | fmd \- \-o \-
.TP
Compare two versions of a document and output visual diff:
.B fmd diff v1.md v2.md \-o diff.html
.TP
Verify accessibility and anchor links in a document:
.B fmd verify document.md \-\-a11y \-\-json
